      "rebaselined": "2026-08-18 T26 / 2026-08-19 A1b. History, kept because the reversal matters: the previous pin (fc6919c2...) was hardware-confirmed WRONG -- it read 0x795fe3dd instead of the 2026-08-02-qualified 0x4147414d, 10 of 32 bits, reproduced 96/96 on an LQFP-100 unit (T23) and again on the L48 reference board (T24), so never unit- or package-specific. T26 traced all ten wrong bits to one shared X14Y8 RMUX->IMUX->RMUX detour (X14Y11_OMUX14->RMUX37->X14Y8_RMUX71->IMUX17->RMUX69), which remains an OPEN encoding defect, and additionally proposed an exact chipdb tuple (1;6) for X14Y11_RMUX03->X13Y11_BBMUXE09 because that value byte-reproduces the retained 2026-08-02 golden (b2047ed2...). A1b REFUTED that proposal on hardware: byte-matching an old golden is not evidence of encoding correctness. Matched A/B on the L48 board, one session -- mcu_ahb_public32_gpio5_w1c_exact_map packed with the fallback (2;4) is the 2026-08-15 silicon golden bc338504... and PASSES (nine error groups zero, ID32 0x4147414d), while the same netlist packed with (1;6) is 8673ae0d... and FAILS with ID32 0x4107414d (0x00400000 = bit 22, exactly the lane BBMUXE09 feeds, which is live in that design); the constant slave reads 0x4147414d BOTH ways, so (1;6) was merely harmless here and wrong there. The tuple was dropped and 48cda69's fallback stands. THIS PIN is the (2;4) image, packed from the retained 2026-08-02 (f705d28) 156-pip routed netlist and read on the physical L48 reference board in that same session: 72/72 direct reads and 6/6 mailbox reads of 0x4147414d, FCB_STAT 0x000f0002 and DEVICE_ID 0x40200001 every cycle, SRAM-only, board left clean. It is therefore a hardware-verified checkpoint, not a fresh-route trip-wire: a truly fresh `agamemnon build --uarch` of this design is NOT guaranteed correct, because nextpnr's route choice drifted since 2026-08-02 purely from chipdb/table growth (same cap=2 seed=4) onto the open X14Y8 detour. Evidence: qualification/mcu_ahb_constant_slave_evidence.jsonl trials 2026-08-18-t26-regression-fix and 2026-08-19-a1b-codeword-matched-ab; board scripts in AG32-Docs/tools/t26_codeword_ab/.",
